{% set local_problem %}
<p>Meridianville homes are surrounded by trees — it's part of what makes the area so appealing. But those beautiful pines and hardwoods are constantly shedding debris into your gutters. Pine needles fall year-round. Oak leaves blanket everything in fall. Sweet gum balls and twigs fill in the gaps.</p>

<p>When gutters clog, water has nowhere to go but over the sides. On Meridianville's sloped lots, that overflow heads straight for your foundation. The result can be erosion, basement moisture, crawlspace problems, and foundation damage — expensive issues that proper gutter maintenance prevents.</p>

<p>Some Meridianville homeowners try to handle gutter cleaning themselves, but climbing ladders on uneven terrain and dealing with two-story heights adds real risk. Professional cleaning is safer, more thorough, and frees up your weekend for better things.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Professional gutter cleaning is straightforward: we remove all debris from your gutters and downspouts, flush the system to ensure proper flow, and inspect for any damage or maintenance needs.</p>

<p>Our process includes: removing leaves, needles, and debris by hand and with specialized tools; checking downspouts for clogs and clearing them; flushing gutters to verify water flow; inspecting for loose hangers, damaged sections, or pitch problems; and cleaning up all debris — we don't leave messes in your yard.</p>

<p>For Meridianville homes with heavy debris, we may recommend more frequent cleaning or discuss gutter guard options that reduce future maintenance.</p>
{% endset %}

